    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      58.92,
      230.54,
      546.22,
      444.77
    ],
    "text": "The Very Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cArnab\u201d over West-central Bay of Bengal lay centered at 11.30 a.m. of today, the 27 October, 2026, near Latitude 16.0\u00b0N and Longitude 84.3\u00b0E about 820 km to the north-east of Kankasanthurai. Thereafter, it is very likely to cross the Indian land through Andhra Pradesh as a very severe cyclonic storm around 11.30 a.m. on the 28th. Wind speeds in the sea areas bounded by 10N to 20N latitude and 80E to 90E longitude may increase to 80-100 kmph at times, heavy thundershowers can occur, the wave height may increase about (3.0 \u2013 4.0) meters in the mentioned sea areas and the sea conditions in these areas will become very rough. Therefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the above mentioned sea areas until further notice. Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move away from the affected sea areas. The naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the Department of Meteorology in this regard.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.039999961853027,
      12.0
    ]
  },
